  <h3 id="multi-model">Orchestrating multiple models and hybrid systems</h3>
  <p>
    The last bullet of the skill: "orchestrate multiple models, flows, or hybrid LLM and rules engines". The patterns
    worth naming:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Model routing / cascading</strong> — a cheap small model handles the easy majority and escalates hard cases to a larger model. The standard answer to "cut cost without losing quality".</li>
    <li><strong>Specialist models per stage</strong> — embeddings for retrieval, a reasoning model for planning, a fast model for the user-facing reply.</li>
    <li><strong>Hybrid LLM + rules</strong> — deterministic business rules decide anything regulated or numeric; the model handles language. If a question involves eligibility, pricing or compliance thresholds, <strong>the rules engine decides and the model explains</strong> — never the reverse.</li>
    <li><strong>Gateway-level orchestration</strong> — Azure API Management as an AI gateway for load balancing across deployments and regions, token limits and quota enforcement.</li>
  </ul>

  <Callout type="exam" title="Skill 2 rapid-fire review">
    <ul style="margin-bottom:0">
      <li>Prompt agent = declarative and fully managed. Hosted agent = your container, plus container compute cost. Responses API direct = ephemeral, no agent resource.</li>
      <li><strong>Conversations</strong> hold <strong>items</strong>; <code>previous_response_id</code> is the lightweight alternative.</li>
      <li><strong>Function calling executes client-side</strong>, which is why it cannot live in a toolbox.</li>
      <li>Toolbox = one MCP endpoint, central auth, guardrails, versioning; update tools without redeploying agents.</li>
      <li><strong>Tool search</strong> solves "too many tools inflate the context window and confuse selection".</li>
      <li>Handoff transfers ownership; agent-as-tool returns control.</li>
      <li>Irreversible actions → <strong>approval-required tools</strong> plus <strong>checkpointing</strong> for long waits.</li>
      <li>Fabrication → groundedness. Wrong tool → tool call accuracy. Misunderstood → intent resolution.</li>
      <li>Tune <strong>temperature or top_p, not both</strong>; an inflated <code>max_output_tokens</code> causes 429s.</li>
      <li>Grounding with Bing sends data <strong>outside the Azure compliance boundary</strong>.</li>
    </ul>
  </Callout>
